         measured: max |K/3H - 1| = 4.79e-03
         reading:  K does not separate bound regions from the Hubble flow: a K-only gate is blind in C-H/K's window (it would need a threshold tuned to this precision at every z, and the sign flips across each region).  DE1's K = 3H assumption at the galaxy stands

==============================================================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================================================
  The khronon's lambda-term makes K harmonic on every leaf (K1), so a static bound region has K = 3H(z) exactly at linear
  order: its leaves are constant-mean-curvature, the tilt pi absorbing the matter's non-expansion.  A moving region
  sources K only through L340's momentum channel, at first order in its speed (K2), and at the gate edges of a 1e11 galaxy
  and a 1e14 cluster at z = 0.25 and 2.5 the deviation is at most 5e-03 of 3H, a dipole (K3).  So a gate on K alone
  cannot tell bound regions from the Hubble flow: the door DE7 found is blind within L340's window.  The curvature gate's
  K = 3H input (DE1) stands.  Time 2 s.

